  "assumptions": [
    "Only the two pure-blue (RGB 0,0,1) stroked paths were digitised; blue is drawn after the grey shading and after the red/green curves, so nothing of the blue is hidden.",
    "The blue paths are PDF-clipped to the axes rectangle; path points outside that rectangle are not visible and were discarded rather than extrapolated.",
    "Points are sampled on a uniform 1.0 pt x-grid (max step 0.0073 dex in log10(mass)); all points lie on the drawn polyline, none are invented.",
    "The excluded region is a closed band bounded by the two edges; both edges are reported because both are drawn blue and both are physical (upper edge = prompt/large-coupling side, lower edge = long-lived side).",
    "At the extreme right tip the path doubles back on itself over ~3.3 pt (the band closes), so theta2 at m_S=62 GeV is uncertain by about 0.1 dex; the mean of the doubled segment is used.",
    "Axis calibration uses the 5 major x ticks and the 4 major y ticks; the minor ticks agree with a pure log scale to <0.01 pt."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "The CSV has no branch column (schema fixed at curve_id,mass_GeV,theta2), so each curve is written as contiguous blocks: lower edge first (mass ascending), then upper edge (mass ascending). Row ranges are given in curves.<id>.segments[].row_start/row_end. Concatenating the blocks with a line would draw a fake connector between them.",
    "The dashed upper edge has two blocks because it leaves the top of the plot for 1.09 < m_S < 1.51 GeV.",
    "The \"Excluded\" text is drawn after the blue and slightly overlaps the upper edges near m_S ~ 1.5-2.5 GeV in the raster, which can bias pixel-based checks there; the vector route is unaffected."
  ]
}